```cpp
void reverse() {
    Node* prev = nullptr;
    Node* c = head;
    while (c) {
        c->next = prev;
        prev = c;
        c = c->next;
    }
    head = prev;
}
```
Bug: `c->next = prev; prev = c; c = c->next;` — after `c->next = prev`, then `c = c->next` sets c to prev, which is wrong! We lost the original next. Fix: save next first.
```cpp
void reverse() {
    Node* prev = nullptr;
    Node* c = head;
    while (c) {
        Node* next = c->next;
        c->next = prev;
        prev = c;
        c = next;
    }
    head = prev;
}
```

